   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-074",
   "status_as_recorded": "rejected",
   "finding": "Gravity persistence test of elite creators on teammate PPP at lags 1-3. All 8 creators at horizon 0; Jokic lag-1 ATT=+0.0282, CI[-0.043,+0.099], p=0.3779. Recorded as a clean null with adequate power (n=1880 for Jokic lag-1). A secondary Antetokounmpo distinct-initiator result (perm p=0.0002, BH 0.003) was marked as structure not effect, with the text cut."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF40",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Descriptive catalogue of same-player and teammate X->Y play-type sequence PPP premiums above baseline (e.g., P. George DRIVE->SPOT_UP +0.560, n=31, t=+2.2; most cells recorded as DIRECT). Limited by label or classification error and small sample."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-034",
   "status_as_recorded": "no result recorded",
   "finding": "Exploratory position and Gobert sanity check on structural load using initiation totals. No result CSV or log was found; the verdict is recorded as abandoned, with failure type E_unclear and confidence low (0.15)."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-074",
   "what_failed": "Testing whether elite creators' signature actions raise teammate PPP over subsequent possessions (lineup-matched, lags 1-3).",
   "why": "Recorded as an adequately powered null (B_powered_null); no elite creator produced a positive lift at any lag. Shows that a gravity-style teammate-lift approach did not detect teammate gains in this data."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-034",
   "what_failed": "Exploratory group comparison of structural load by position and low initiation volume.",
   "why": "No result was recorded; the output tables were not found and the mechanism is unclear (E_unclear). Abandoned."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF40",
   "what_failed": "Sequence-level premium estimates for play-type pairs.",
   "why": "Mechanism unclear; limited by label or classification error and small cell sizes (n around 30-70), so premiums are not established as hypothesis tests."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Earlier work in this project has used the same play-by-play-derived initiation and PPP machinery and has found usage and identity effects of absence and connector roles (FAM:SF-APPS-088).",
  "A lineup-matched teammate-PPP lift from elite creators was not detected at any lag (FAM:SF-APPS-074), so teammate gains in this framework are not a given.",
  "Descriptive play-type sequence premiums exist but are small-sample and label-sensitive (FAM:SF40)."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "Nothing retrieved tests whether the closest pre-absence initiation-profile teammate is the largest gainer in the absent player's primary play types.",
  "No retrieved record reports per-absence teammate gain rankings or a profile-similarity measure.",
  "FAM:SF-APPS-088 measures team identity displacement (D_A), not teammate gains by play type, so it does not answer the ranking question.",
  "The retrieved records do not establish how many absence cases are needed for a ranking test."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "The effective sample for the question is 11 absence cases, not 148 spells. Spells from the same absent player are clustered, so the 148 spells overstate the information available for a ranking claim.",
